WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.277
UNION ALL is a straightforward unpivot pattern.

00:00:03.277 --> 00:00:06.382
Write one SELECT for each source column.

00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:09.307
Give each SELECT the same output structure.

00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:11.927
Then stack the rows with UNION ALL.

00:00:11.927 --> 00:00:18.087
This is verbose but very beginner-friendly because each source column is visible in its own SELECT.

00:00:18.087 --> 00:00:21.767
Unpivoting turns repeated columns into row values.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:27.872
UNION ALL is explicit and portable; LATERAL VALUES can be more compact in PostgreSQL.

00:00:27.872 --> 00:00:34.732
The important design decision is which columns become identifiers and which column names become values.

00:00:34.732 --> 00:00:37.840
Keep data types compatible across the generated rows.
